# What CloudFront's ResponseHeadersPolicy used to attach, in the form
# Cloudflare Pages reads. The headers are the same ones the SAM template
# declared; only the thing that sends them changed. Vite copies everything in
# public/ to the root of dist/ untouched, which is what Pages looks for.
#
# HSTS because the app is HTTPS-only from here on, and a bearer token in
# localStorage is worth saying so about.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Every file under assets/ carries a content hash in its name, so a changed
# file is a different name and this can never serve a stale one. index.html is
# deliberately left out: Pages revalidates it on every request, and that is
# what makes a new deploy visible without an invalidation to buy.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
